diff --git a/docs/business-rules.md b/docs/business-rules.md
index 7a3126a..9d8ac0f 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -63,7 +63,21 @@ ## User Administration
 | Reset password | Admin, owner | Reset flow for **account** (login) and **user** (entity member), per security policy. |
 | Remove account | Admin, owner | Not applicable to owner while being owner. |
 | Remove user | Admin, owner | Cannot remove the owner; employees lose immediate access to the entity. |
-| Assign role | Admin, owner | Users are **separated by role**; employees receive granular permissions, not admin/owner role. |
+| Assign role | Admin, owner | Users are **separated by role**; employees receive granular permissions, not admin/owner role. Changed from the member details modal with an explicit save; the owner's role never changes there. |
+| Invite user | Admin, owner | Invite-only: see [Invitations](#invitations). |
+
+### Invitations
+
+Membership is **invite-only**: nobody is added to an entity without accepting an invite.
+
+- A manager (owner or admin) invites an e-mail address with the role `admin` or `employee`. The **owner role is never invitable**; ownership moves only by transfer.
+- The invitee receives an e-mail and answers in the app, after signing in (or registering) with that address. Matching is case-insensitive. Accepting creates the membership with the invited role; declining deletes the invite.
+- An invite **expires after 7 days**. It is **pending** while it is neither accepted nor expired.
+- An address that already belongs to a member cannot be invited. A second pending invite for the same address in the same entity is refused. An expired or previously accepted invite may be replaced by a new one.
+- Accepting an invite when the membership already exists keeps the existing membership and role.
+- Managers may cancel pending invites of their entity.
+- Rate limit: a manager may send **10 successful invites per entity per hour**. Invalid input does not use up the quota.
+- Out of scope for now: signed invite links or tokens, resending invites, inviting one address to several entities at once.
 
 ## Queue and Tickets
 
